-- Q1304: International Tax [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): With a 37.5% Section 250 deduction, the taxable portion of GILTI is 62.5% (100% minus 37.5%). Applying the 21% corporate rate yields an effective GILTI rate of 13.125% (21% times 62.5%). This represents an increase from the prior 10.5% effective rate when the deduction was 50%.
Wrong (A): 10.5% was the effective GILTI rate when the Section 250 deduction was 50% (21% times 50%), which applied for tax years before 2026.
Wrong (C): 15.75% would result from a 25% deduction (21% times 75%), but Section 250 provides a 37.5% deduction, not 25%.
Wrong (D): 21% would apply only if no Section 250 deduction were available, but GILTI receives the 37.5% deduction.$EXPL$
